# Minuet in G minor, BWV Anh. 115 (attributed to Christian Petzold)
#
# From the 1725 Notebook for Anna Magdalena Bach (No. 5), the companion
# of the G major Minuet (No. 4). Usually attributed to Christian Petzold
# (1677-1733), as the Mutopia score notes; not by J. S. Bach.
#
# Character: the minor-key partner of the G major minuet, more inward.
# A falling opening phrase (B-flat, A, G) over a bass descending by step,
# then running eighths. Two voices, the bass in halves and quarters.
#
# Time signature: 3/4, 32 bars in the Mutopia score and in the MIDI
# (16 + 16, each half repeated); the first note is on the downbeat.
# The MIDI does not play the repeats, so they are written out with `play`.
#
# Tempo: quarter = 126 (dotted half = 42). With both repeats it is 64
# bars, 192 quarters. MusicBrainz track times: Pieter-Jan Belder
# (harpsichord) 1:30, about 128; Justin Taylor (harpsichord) 1:31, about
# 127; Igor Kipnis (harpsichord) 1:29, about 129; Kevin Bowyer 1:39,
# about 116 (all assuming both repeats; Benjamin Alard's 1:02 must leave
# some out). 126 follows the harpsichordists, a touch steadier than the
# G major minuet (132) for the minor key.
#
# Structure (my reading of the Mutopia score, after Bach-Gesellschaft):
#   1-8    G minor, falling phrase; half close on D (bar 8, A with a trill)
#   9-16   the phrase again, now turning to B-flat; cadence there (16)
#   17-24  second half in B-flat, rising; cadence in B-flat at bar 24
#   25-28  sequence over B natural and C (D7 to C minor), half close on
#          D at bar 28 (the bass alone, a breath)
#   29-32  the run up and the final cadence in G minor
#
# Bars as performed (after `play`):
#   A first time 1-16, A repeat 17-32, B first time 33-48, B repeat 49-64.
#   Score bar 17+y of B is 33+y and 49+y.
#
# Plan: each half full the first time, echoed softer on the repeat. The
# half close at score bar 28 (after the sequence) gets a small breath;
# the dance otherwise keeps its pulse.

tempo 126
play 1-16 1-16 17-32 17-32

voice mid 1        # the mid voice is only the left hand's thirds and the
                   # final chords: keep it behind the tune

dyn 1 mf           # bars 1-16: A, first time
dyn 17 mp          # bars 17-32: A repeat, an echo
dyn 33 mf          # bars 33-48: B, first time
dyn 49 mp          # bars 49-56: B repeat, an echo ...
dyn 57 mf          # bars 57-64: ... full again from the sequence to the end

broaden 44 0.94    # score bar 28: the half close on D after the sequence
broaden 60 0.94    # and in the repeat

rit 2 0.8          # bars 63-64: the final cadence in G minor
